description:
Parent: CD-y4u0. Depends on Phase B (CD-94ow) since consensus events drive the UI shape.

Surface v4 ensemble decisions in the State Inspector. The new chunk_id patterns from Phase A/B let the existing rail render the right cards automatically:
- `{doc_id}:_ner_<encoder>` — per-encoder NER cards (one per (doc, encoder))
- `{doc_id}:_consensus` — consensus card per doc
- `{doc_id}:{window_id}` — per-evidence-window SPO cards (existing v3 shape)

What's missing is the **detail panel** content for the consensus card. Today it would show the generic chunk-detail view; for v4 it should show:
- Vote breakdown table (one row per consensus mention, with `text · canonical_type · vote_count/N · mean_conf · source_models`)
- Type vote tally per mention (which encoders voted which type)
- Span provenance (which encoder's span won, span_disagreement_chars)
- Rejected mentions section (collapsed by default, expands to show below-quorum drops with the reason)

**Files:**
- New: `packages/media-ingest/viewer-ui/src/components/state/ConsensusDetail.tsx` — the consensus-card detail view
- Modified: `packages/media-ingest/viewer-ui/src/components/state/ChunkTextPanel.tsx` (or its v4 successor) — route to ConsensusDetail when chunk_id ends `:_consensus`
- Modified: `packages/media-ingest/viewer-ui/src/types/benchmark.ts` — add `MentionDecisionEvent` type matching the consensus_started / mention_decision / mention_rejected / consensus_completed event shape

Read the actual emitted event detail shape from `consensus.py::ConsensusNode.__call__` to pin the TypeScript types.</description>
<design>**Detail panel switch** in StateInspector right pane:
```typescript
function rightPaneContent(selectedChunkId, events) {
  if (selectedChunkId.endsWith(":_consensus")) return <ConsensusDetail .../>
  if (selectedChunkId.includes(":_ner_")) return <PerEncoderDetail .../>  // optional polish
  if (selectedChunkId.match(/:win-/)) return <WindowDetail .../>          // existing window detail
  return <DefaultChunkDetail .../>
}
```

**ConsensusDetail layout:**
```
┌─ Consensus for joe-rogan-2284 ─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ encoders: 5 — gliner-medium, gliner-large, gliner-pii, nuextract, uner │
│ accepted: 87 mentions  ·  rejected: 23 (below quorum 3)                │
│ span disagreement rate: 12% (of accepted)                              │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ACCEPTED                                                                │
│ Reagan          PERSON    5/5  conf 0.94  span: gliner-large            │
│   ↳ types: PERSON×5                                                     │
│ Putin           PERSON    4/5  conf 0.87  span: gliner-large            │
│   ↳ types: PERSON×4, GPE×1                                              │
│ Crimea          LOCATION  3/5  conf 0.62  span: nuextract               │
│   ↳ types: LOCATION×3, ORG×1, GPE×1                                     │
│ ...                                                                     │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ▸ REJECTED (23) — click to expand                                       │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Each accepted row is sortable. Group by canonical_type or by vote_count for analysis. Click an entity row → highlights its span in the source-text view (existing pattern).

**MentionDecisionEvent type:**
Match the actual event shape from ConsensusNode (read consensus.py to confirm exact fields):
```typescript
interface MentionDecisionDetails {
  text: string;
  canonical_type: string;
  vote_count: number;
  n_encoders: number;
  source_models: string[];
  mean_confidence: number;
  type_votes: Record<string, number>;
  span_provenance: string;
  span_disagreement_chars: number;
}

interface MentionRejectedDetails {
  text: string;
  vote_count: number;
  n_encoders: number;
  quorum: number;
  reason: string;
  source_models: string[];
  mean_confidence: number;
}

interface ConsensusCompletedDetails {
  accepted_count: number;
  rejected_count: number;
  mean_vote_count: number;
  type_distribution: Record<string, number>;
  span_disagreement_rate: number;
}
```

**Tests** (Playwright + manual):
- Load State Inspector with a v4 events.jsonl fixture, click consensus card, snapshot the detail panel.
- Verify accepted + rejected counts match the event totals.
- Click a vote-1/5 entity, verify the source-text highlight + the span-provenance label.</design>
<acceptance>1. ConsensusDetail.tsx renders the accepted table with text, canonical_type, vote_count/n, mean_conf, span_provenance per row.
2. Type votes summary shown per row (e.g. `PERSON×4, GPE×1`).
3. Rejected section collapsed by default; expanded shows below-quorum mentions + reason.
4. Header summary: encoders list, total accepted, total rejected, span disagreement rate.
5. Right-pane router dispatches to ConsensusDetail when selected chunk_id ends `:_consensus`.
6. TypeScript types match the actual event details emitted by ConsensusNode (verify via grep on consensus.py).
7. yarn lint, tsc --noEmit, yarn build all clean.
8. Playwright snapshot of the consensus card showing real v4 events from a recent run (post Phase E bench).</acceptance>
